---
layout: layouts/topics.njk
# Page assets. Eleventy merges these lists with the directory data
# (content/problems/problems.11tydata.js, which loads players.js and leaves
# solutions.js out for a stand-alone problem).
styles:
  - pages/problem.css
scripts:
  - solutions.js
---
{#-
  Problem page (HANDOFF §6.4, design A; boards Problem-A.dc.html and
  Problem-Phone.dc.html; SPEC §7.2, §9, §12, §15.1). One DOM for every
  width: below 600px CSS shows the back link and the "On this page" chips
  instead of the breadcrumb, runs the problem video full-bleed and shows the
  solution cards as an accordion (src/css/pages/problem.css).

  Order: breadcrumb, H1, the first-person line; the problem block (the
  problem video with its notice and formats, and "Is this you?"); Main
  solutions; "Other things that can help" (only when there are extras);
  Related topics (only when there are some); "Back to all sleep problems".
  Heading outline: h1, then h2 for "Is this you?", each solutions section and
  Related topics, then h3 per solution.

  A stand-alone problem (`standalone: true`, SPEC §7.2, §7.5) has no
  solutions: its own video, made for it, is the page's main content. The
  "On this page" chips and both solutions sections are left out (each needs
  solutions to link to or list), so the page is the problem block, then
  Related topics and "Back to all sleep problems", and
  content/problems/problems.11tydata.js leaves solutions.js out. Each section
  renders from its own count, so no empty section or orphaned heading can
  appear.

  Front matter: SPEC §7.2 (title, statement, area, problem_video, standalone,
  is_this_you, solutions, related). The problem file's body isn't shown.

  Ratings (M4, SPEC §12) have slots under each video and in each closed card;
  they render nothing until then. There is no per-video feedback (SPEC §13):
  the footer's "Send feedback" is the only route.
-#}
{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import icon -%}
{%- from "partials/video.njk" import videoEmbed -%}
{%- from "partials/formats.njk" import formatLinks -%}
{%- from "partials/rating.njk" import rating -%}
{%- from "problem/solutions.njk" import solutionsSection -%}
{%- set problemArea = areas | areaById(area) -%}
{%- set problemVideo = problem_video | videoById(collections.videos) -%}
{%- set tiers = solutions | solutionsByTier(collections.videos) -%}
{%- set ratingsOn = site.features.ratings -%}
{%- set mainCount = tiers.main.length -%}
{%- set extraCount = tiers.extra.length -%}
{%- set thisIsYou = is_this_you or {} -%}
{%- set bullets = thisIsYou.bullets or [] -%}
<div class="problem">
  <div class="problem__top">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol role="list">
        <li><a href="/problems/">Sleep problems</a></li>
        <li><span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span><a href="/problems/#{{ area }}">{{ problemArea.name }}</a></li>
        <li><span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span><span aria-current="page">{{ title }}</span></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <a class="problem__back" href="/problems/#{{ area }}">{{ icon('chevron-left', 16) }}<span class="visually-hidden">Back to </span>{{ problemArea.name }}</a>
    <div class="problem__head">
      <h1 class="problem__title">{{ title }}</h1>
      <p class="problem__statement">“{{ statement | sentence }}”</p>
    </div>
    {%- if mainCount %}
    <nav class="on-this-page" aria-label="On this page">
      <ul role="list">
        <li><a class="on-this-page__lead" href="#about-this">About this</a></li>
        <li><a href="#main-solutions">{{ mainCount }} main solution{{ 's' if mainCount != 1 }}</a></li>
        {%- if extraCount %}
        <li><a href="#more-solutions">{{ extraCount }} more<span class="visually-hidden"> solution{{ 's' if extraCount != 1 }}</span></a></li>
        {%- endif %}
      </ul>
    </nav>
    {%- endif %}
    <div class="problem-block" id="about-this">
      <div class="problem-block__video">
        {{ videoEmbed(problemVideo, showTitle=true, bleed='page', arc=true) }}
        {#- M4: the SPEC §12 ratings widget renders here (nothing until then). #}
        {%- if ratingsOn %}{{ rating(problemVideo, page_id, 'row') }}{% endif %}
        {{ formatLinks(problemVideo) }}
      </div>
      {%- if thisIsYou.summary or bullets.length %}
      <div class="is-this-you panel panel--wash">
        <h2 class="is-this-you__title" id="is-this-you-title">Is this you?</h2>
        {%- if thisIsYou.summary %}
        <p class="is-this-you__summary">{{ thisIsYou.summary }}</p>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if bullets.length %}
        <p class="is-this-you__lead">This topic may help if you:</p>
        <ul class="is-this-you__list">
          {%- for bullet in bullets %}
          <li>{{ bullet }}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        {%- endif %}
        {%- if related and related.length %}
        {%- set nextTopic = related[0] | problemBySlug(collections.problems) %}
        <p class="is-this-you__next">Not quite? Try <a href="{{ nextTopic.url }}">{{ nextTopic.title }}</a>.</p>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      {%- endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if mainCount %}

  {{ solutionsSection('main', tiers.main, page_id, ratingsOn) }}
  {%- endif %}

  {%- if extraCount %}

  {{ solutionsSection('extra', tiers.extra, page_id, ratingsOn) }}
  {%- endif %}

  <div class="problem__end">
    {%- if related and related.length %}
    <section class="related" aria-labelledby="related-title">
      <h2 class="related__title" id="related-title">Related topics</h2>
      <ul class="related__list" role="list">
        {%- for slug in related %}
        {%- set topic = slug | problemBySlug(collections.problems) %}
        <li><a class="topic-card" href="{{ topic.url }}"><span class="topic-card__title">{{ topic.title }}</span> <span class="topic-card__statement">{{ topic.statement }}</span></a></li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
    {%- endif %}
    <p class="problem__all"><a href="/problems/">Back to all sleep problems</a></p>
  </div>
</div>
